  "notes": "West leads the ♥10 against 3NT. East wins the ♥A and returns the suit to South. South has 8 top tricks (the ♠A, 3 hearts, and 4 diamonds). South's only chance for a ninth trick is to finesse East for the ♣A.\n\nIf South continues with a spade to dummy's ♠A and leads a club toward the ♣K, East will take the ♣A and the defense will win 3 spade tricks to defeat the contract. South can guard against this danger and make his contract whenever East was dealt no more than 3 spades (along with the ♣A that is required for South to have a chance).\n\nSouth should duck a spade at trick 3. The defense can do no better than to put South back in his hand, but a second spade duck will sever the defenders' communications in that suit. Declarer can win any return and play a spade to the ♠A. East can win the ♣A when South leads toward his ♣K, but with the long spade in the West hand, the contract is safe.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥10 against 3NT. East wins the ♥A and returns the suit to South. South has 8 top tricks (the ♠A, 3 hearts, and 4 diamonds). South's only chance for a ninth trick is to finesse East for the ♣A.",
    "If South continues with a spade to dummy's ♠A and leads a club toward the ♣K, East will take the ♣A and the defense will win 3 spade tricks to defeat the contract. South can guard against this danger and make his contract whenever East was dealt no more than 3 spades (along with the ♣A that is required for South to have a chance).",
    "South should duck a spade at trick 3. The defense can do no better than to put South back in his hand, but a second spade duck will sever the defenders' communications in that suit. Declarer can win any return and play a spade to the ♠A. East can win the ♣A when South leads toward his ♣K, but with the long spade in the West hand, the contract is safe."
  ],
